      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "All features listed have been implemented now. Smoothed pinned transitions work well when switching from World/Local to Default (Camera) space pins, but the reverse either snaps or transitions from the previous position to the current position of the same pin. No defined time for the transition.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-01-18T15:58:43.900Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "-Changeable zoom/FOV, allowing for both far shots but also wide angle photos. preferably as a toggle-able slider but set buttons for wide angle, zoom and normal would be alright too\n-Depending on camera rotation auto correct the saved picture\n-A grid in the viewfinder, the usual rule of thirds would do the job\n-Leveling tools so that the camera can be leveled with the push of a button\n-Higher resolution output, 1080p is fine as is but a 4K resolution would make post processing work far easier to deal with\nOne more thing that could be added for the stream camera, when switching between pinned cameras have it be a smooth transition. Obviously give the user the option to toggle it and maybe even set the transition duration.",
